\"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"f322bddccf828531a123388c301cfd16a1dcd74313048ff2bc52fd625527ce67","event_uuid":"1b6db08b-0cea-4653-9495-aafaf75d1cbb","position":{"commit_sha":"1cf17d7536dc6627ad51ca93ac3f431f3252d6e7","position":"1795116813219754565-1b6db08b-0cea-4653-9495-aafaf75d1cbb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Decomposition (cluster T1, 2026-11-19 PST). Children in landing order, each its own Gerrit change:\n1. calcite-cursed-lovebird — ADR 0125 records the decision and supersedes ADR 0049's pinning (and the ADR 0104 decision-3 dependency). Epic AC 1.\n2. unequaled-sincere-firefly — adds `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` (entries `<env_id> <key-type> <base64> [comment]`, env `REBAR_VERIFY_TRUSTED_OPCERT_KEYS`, `mechanism-ok` marker naming this epic), the `untrusted` verdict and `signing_key` report, and sets the 3 current keys in the MCP deployment (compose `mcp` service + autodeploy `mcp_run_new`). Epic AC 4 and 5.\n3. notorious-deadsmooth-rattail — validity-only default; signing, health and `verify-opcert` stop reading the pin file. Epic AC 3.\n4. prosaic-visionary-basilisk — deletes `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`, `attest/trusted_env.py` and `rebar trusted-env`. Epic AC 2.\n5. waterish-aquamarine-bug — docs and runbooks, including `infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md`.\nEpic AC 6 (make verify + Gerrit votes) is met per child.\n\nOrder change versus the requested \"core → config\" sequence: the config setting and the MCP deployment list land together BEFORE the core change. If the core change landed first, the live MCP server would run validity-only (no list) between the two deploys. With this order the server always has either the pin file or its own list.\n\nDesign choices made within scope (one line each):\n- Trust-list entries bind a key to an environment id, mirroring the operator's env→keys listing; a listed key presented under a different principal is `untrusted`.\n- `verify.require_environment` keeps its meaning and now requires a trust list, since a principal alone is a self-claim; without one it refuses (`foreign_key`), preserving today's \"no self-certification under enforcement\" property.\n- Keys in the list carry no eras; removing a key untrusts every certificate it signed.\n- Review-bot and developer clones get no list and become validity-only, per the default.","timestamp":1795112782690480170}],"created_at":1795111375767735238,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Operator decision (2026-11-19 PST)\nOp-cert keys must not be hardcoded in the repository. Remove `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` and the machinery that pins op-cert keys in the repo.\n\n- **Default behaviour:** op-cert verification checks only that a certificate's signature is valid and binds the certificate. It reports which key and environment produced the certificate. It does not check whether that key is trusted.\n- **Per-environment trust:** a specific environment may define the certificates it trusts. For example, an MCP server can be configured to trust only its own signatures. Trust lives in that environment's own configuration, not in the repository.\n- **Rebar's own MCP server** is configured with the current trusted list: env 9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65 (keys `nava-opcert-prod` and `nava-opcert-prod rotated-20260907`) and env ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5 (`rebar-opcert`).\n\nPrinciple (operator, 2026-11-19): identity, authorization and op-cert certification are separate. Anyone can sign a plan review, code review or completion verification. Identity can be verified separately.\n\n## Scope\n1. A new ADR that supersedes ADR 0049's repo pinning (and the related part of ADR 0104), recording this decision.\n2. Remove `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml`, `rebar trusted-env`, and repo-pinned trust lookups. Rework `verify-opcert`, `_opcert_verify.py`, `attest/trusted_env.py` and `_mcp_opcert_health.py` so that the default is validity-only.\n3. Add the per-environment trust setting. It is optional, unset means validity-only, and it is documented in docs/config.md with a `mechanism-ok` marker.\n4. Configure rebar's MCP server deployment with the current trusted list.\n5. Update docs and the runbooks that reference the pinned file, including `infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The ADR superseding ADR 0049's pinning has merged.\n- [ ] `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` and `rebar trusted-env` no longer exist on main, and no code reads a repo-pinned op-cert trust file.\n- [ ] With no trust setting, op-cert verification passes a validly signed certificate from any key, fails a tampered or wrongly bound certificate, and reports the signing key and environment.\n- [ ] With a trust setting, a certificate signed by a key outside the list is reported as untrusted, and a certificate signed by a listed key passes.\n- [ ] Rebar's MCP server runs with the trust setting listing the 3 current keys, and its `/health` op-cert check passes after deploy.\n- [ ] `make verify` is green, and the changes land through Gerrit with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"1af77924-fa84-4486-8222-b0ac2dd4d1c2","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0dd0-cecb-3932-4c90","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Op-cert trust: verify validity by default; per-environment trust lists replace the repo-pinned trusted_environments.yaml","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3f314a7d-6c91-4329-928c-189606a48d36","ce5f1610-086f-4374-a422-fdaf89952d6a","3add8662-0fb6-42f8-b181-0e6b02bd2548","1af77924-fa84-4486-8222-b0ac2dd4d1c2","1b6db08b-0cea-4653-9495-aafaf75d1cbb"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795116813219754566,"uuid":"b1d05a5c-bbcd-44e4-86fc-519cf6d1eb0b"}